## 4. Notification protocol

- Workers notify the Orchestrator when blocked, when a design decision is required, when review is ready, when integration is ready, and when complete.
- Reviewers notify the paired Worker and Orchestrator with the review path and verdict.
- The Orchestrator owns pause/resume decisions, shared-ownership windows, and root GOAL updates.
- A task-model handshake does not configure nested subagents; each explicit subagent configuration and context mode needs its own receipt.
